<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Auto Backup rules for Android 11 and below (android:fullBackupContent).

     The Wallhaven API key is encrypted with a key that lives in the Android
     Keystore, and the Keystore is never backed up. Backing up the encrypted
     blob alone would restore a secret that nothing on the new device can
     decrypt — which surfaces as a corrupt key, not a missing one. Leave it
     behind instead: an absent key is a state the app already handles (it asks
     for one), and re-pasting it is a five-second job.

     The second exclusion is the private library itself: `filesDir/wallpapers`
     is the app-private storage tier (TelaDirectories.privateImages), whose
     whole promise in PLAN.md is that only tela can see those images and that
     they go with an uninstall. Auto Backup is on by default, so without this
     line every private image is copied into the user's Google account — the
     exact exposure the tier exists to prevent, and the one the v5 migration
     already acted on for the *rows* pointing at these files while the files
     themselves stayed eligible.

     Nothing else needs a line. The decoded previews live under `cacheDir`
     (TelaDirectories.previews), and Auto Backup never carries the cache
     directory. Everything that remains — the Drift database, the download
     destinations — backs up normally, and holds no private-tier entry by
     construction: see DownloadedWallpapers' docstring. -->
<full-backup-content>
    <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="FlutterSecureStorage.xml"/>
    <exclude domain="file" path="wallpapers"/>
</full-backup-content>
